- Verification suite: the repo's own `tests/dbshell/test_postgresql.py` is the pre-fix version (it mocks `subprocess.call`/`check_call` and reads `PGPASSFILE`), and the task forbids touching tests — so I ran a throwaway mirror of the upstream post-fix tests in `C:/Windows/Temp/pgverify/test_new.py` (basic → `PGPASSWORD` passed via env; nopass → no password env; SIGINT handler ignored during run and restored after): **Ran 3 tests … OK** against the refactored client.
- Environment note: the campaign venv has no pytest (`No module named pytest`), and `runtests.py` needs `PYTHONPATH=.`; the in-repo pre-fix tests fail under the new code for the expected reason (they invoke real `psql` instead of a mock) — not a defect of the fix.

